    "summary": "The private M0-A interview path is deployed through acknowledged-batch proposal admission, value-minimized review composition, partial acceptance for selected ordinary batch Candidates, individual terminal review for sensitive or explicitly single-review Candidates, a separate default-off iOS QA review consumer, a deployed value-minimized interview-session state read, and a lease-bound typed iOS natural-input client. The existing QA keyboard entry remains double-gated. A product natural-input surface is G0/G1 verified: it starts hidden in the existing full-screen Echo, requires both a fresh route visibility and write decision for echoTextInput, clears immediately on account rebind, and uses product wording without internal QA details. Formal backend writes require a captured server release-policy decision and reject absent policy without falling back to QA. `db95a5f` deployed the input authorization path; `8cb6a0d` deployed a content-free continuation presentation route and its isolated Postgres smoke verified rejected missing capture, matching capture, and presentation semantics without production business-data mutation. The product Sheet maps only server state to a natural summary and never exposes input text, Candidate content, review IDs, pacing, fatigue, or internal session details. Both UIQA surfaces use in-memory clients and never perform a private write, voice turn, or Digital Human request. `79a0504` added a separately policy-gated confirmation read route; iOS has a typed, lease-fenced, default-off read consumer that reuses the captured product policy and never carries the QA header or a decision mutation. `a9efa24` adds the separate formal batch-accept route under the confirmation path: it is default-off, requires a fresh captured `ownerTruthCandidateReview` policy, cannot be bypassed by a QA header, fixes the server-side boundary-confirmation reason, returns no Candidate content or QA receipt envelope, and records terminal Candidate receipts without activating a MemoryVersion. M0A-20 adds a separate typed iOS action consumer for that formal route: it remains fail-closed, validates AccountLease at request and commit, permits only ordinary batch Candidates present in the confirmation projection, rejects single/sensitive Candidate IDs, reuses a command ID for an unchanged retry, rejects QA response envelopes, and discards stale deferred results after account rebind. M0A-21 requires a fresh formal confirmation read after action success and enters confirmed only when every accepted Candidate has disappeared from the refreshed projection; a failed reconciliation preserves the value-minimized action result but does not claim completion. M0A-22 additionally binds a successfully read confirmation projection to the exact AccountLease that passed its completion fence and rejects a reconciliation whose admission/source/version/authority epoch drifts, while allowing candidate membership to change after a decision. `a954ac9` adds hash-minimized formal authorization evidence and immutable root-to-terminal receipt links; migration `0036` is deployed and `/ready` is healthy, while the deliberately isolated formal Postgres route smoke remains pending a dedicated disposable-database connection. Neither slice adds UI or a release entry. The next task is an evidence gap audit for existing `WI-S1-01-04` review authority rather than exposing these internal consumers. QA Candidate review routes remain unavailable to product code. Registry status remains deliberately conservative."
